<title>CHINA: China Jan crude oil imports up, exports down.</title>
<headline>China Jan crude oil imports up, exports down.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China imported 1.57 million tonnes of crude oil in January, up 21.7 percent from the year-ago period, the International Business Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>China's oil imports were 22.62 million tonnes in 1996, up 32.3 percent compared with 1995, customs figures showed.</p>
<p>China's crude oil exports in January reached 850,000 tonnes, down 35.1 percent against the year-ago period, the newspaper said, quoted customs figures.</p>
<p>Exports in 1996 were 20.33 million tonnes, up 7.9 percent compared with 1995, customs figures showed.</p>
</text>
